80 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (Qwen was used as an additional language-model experiment. I used the 3B version because larger versions caused GPU memory and bitsandbytes compatibility problems on Kaggle. This model was much heavier than BiLSTM and DeBERTa, so it was useful mainly for comparison.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
81 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (The goal of this project was to build a model that can solve multiple-choice questions. Each question has five options \(A-E\). The model has to rank the most likely answers, and the Kaggle score is based on MAP@3. This means the correct answer should appear as high as possible in the top three predictions.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [29]
>>
endobj
82 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (My main goal was to understand the full deep learning workflow: preparing text data, training different models, comparing them, tracking experiments, making a Kaggle submission, and finally deploying one trained model as a small web app.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
