/T (The BiLSTM score of 1.0 on the validation set is unusually high, so I do not assume it will generalize perfectly. The Kaggle leaderboard is a better test of unseen performance. The notebook also searched ensemble weights using trained-model probabilities only. The best validation MAP@3 was 0.99717 with weights 0.40 BiLSTM, 0.10 DeBERTa, and 0.50 Qwen. My final public Kaggle score was about 0.75394, which is above the required 0.73 cutoff. The exact leaderboard rank is not stored in the notebook, so I have not added a made-up rank.)
