/T (7. Evaluation The main competition metric was MAP@3. I also used accuracy and macro-F1 during validation. MAP@3 is useful here because it gives the highest reward when the correct option is ranked first, a smaller reward when it is second or third, and zero if it is outside the top three. My final Kaggle public leaderboard score was about 0.75394, which was above the required 0.73 cutoff. The final  submission used trained-model probabilities only.)
